WEBVTT

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:09.440
Th-This is the hospital where Taniguchi-san's 
husband was brought after he was infected.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:09.970
m 0 0 l 400 0 l 400 22 l 0 22

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:09.970
<b>Keimon City Central Ward Hospital #3</b>

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.260
This is where Japan's pandemic started.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.520
It's completely abandoned.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.630
No! No! I'm scared!

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.010
Ghosts are the only thing that scare me!

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:56.260
I want to go home!

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.110
Sui-chan, I guess there is something that 
scares you even though you're so strong.

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:01.180
It's still the middle of the day. 
You'll be fine.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.520
I don't see anything that could be a clue.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.890
We can't find out how he was infected.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:13.950
We don't know where he was or what 
he was doing before it started.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:17.780
The infected all appeared around 
the world at the same time, right?

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:21.970
<i>Is this a refugee area, too?</i>

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:27.160
Are the leaders of UW only interested 
in what happens in the core?

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:33.100
They're doing their best to bring 
back the men in cold sleep.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.900
Are they?

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:39.260
A ghost!

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.390
Okay, say "aah."

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:52.000
I never expected Rika-senpai, the most 
popular girl at my old part-time job,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.060
to be willing to feed me like that.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.950
I'm so happy.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.570
You're flattering me.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.150
I'm not.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:03.820
Kyouji-sama, are you thirsty?

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.080
Yeah.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.470
Hey, let me join in...

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.340
I'll satisfy you all.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.670
<i>I'm happy.</i>

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.730
<i>But when it's the same thing every day,</i>

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.820
<i>I do get bored...</i>

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:43.560
<i>I want something new.</i>

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:49.500
Oh, there you are.

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.440
What's this about?

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.960
I thought it would do our relationship 
good to get naked together.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.630
You and I haven't had a chance to talk.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.550
You're barbaric.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.730
We're both girls. We don't 
need to hide anything.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.810
If you want to say something, say it.

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.260
I'm leaving.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:09.890
About Taniguchi...

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.260
I looked at her medical records and 
the logs of her life support device.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.140
Taniguchi Emi

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:19.410
And the way the numbers 
changed made no sense.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:23.780
Somebody poisoned her.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.400
If that's true, it's a serious concern.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.030
We'll have to look into that.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.540
I'm not done!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.910
Don't touch me.

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:38.630
What were you doing that night?

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.930
Writing my report to my bosses.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:47.390
I need to tell them what 
Mizuhara Reito's doing.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.350
Was there someone with you?

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:50.920
No.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:54.010
But you don't have the 
right to question me.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:05.200
Ryuuzouji-san, you seem very 
concerned about Director Kihara.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:07.500
You...

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.160
I'll return this to you.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.710
There was nothing unusual about it.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.830
You needed to scrutinize a photo stand?

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.320
I-I'm sorry...

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.970
But we had to make sure it didn't 
have bacteria on it or anything.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:28.340
<i>Why did Taniguchi-san want me to have this?</i>

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:31.580
<i>You'll give up on the girl you love?</i>

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.220
<i>Erisa...</i>

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:38.510
<i>The ring...</i>

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:42.230
This is where my little 
sister goes to high school.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.220
m 0 0 l 20 0 l 20 280 l 0 280

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.220
K
e
i
m
o
n

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.040
You have a sister?

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:47.990
She's much younger than me and we 
didn't live together much, but...

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:52.060
She's very smart. She skipped 
grades to get to high school.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.740
Why not meet her while we're here?

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:57.810
No, she's busy with studying, I'm sure.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.990
<b>Keimon City West</b>

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.870
Kamiya-san? What's wrong?

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:07.130
Nothing, Yuzu-sensei.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.290
Let's go.

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:10.880
Yes.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:21.950
Looks like it worked.

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:22.900
Great!

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:27.140
It's nice to get a chance to 
go outside and pick a girl.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.600
Thanks for the idea, Neneko-chan.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:31.670
I'm glad you liked it.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:34.940
Stop the car!

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:36.000
What's wrong?

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:36.980
Her!

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:40.000
The one with the pigtails 
who's holding that kid's hand!

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:44.640
I love her smile! 
I'd like to mate with her.

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:45.880
She's a little young, but...

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.170
<i>That girl is...</i>

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.380
We need to hurry or we'll lose her!

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:51.890
Wow, things are looking stormy.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.860
They're both reacting to each other?

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.080
<i>This paper...</i>

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:05.140
<b>Development of an Artificial Male Killer Virus</b>

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:04.240
<i>It's about how to make the MK Virus!</i>

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:08.070
<i>The MK Virus was artificially made!</i>

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.820
<i>This is the information 
Erisa was talking about...</i>

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:12.970
<i>Why would Taniguchi-san have it?</i>

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:18.130
<i>Did she not tell UW about 
her husband because</i>

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:20.380
<i>she didn't want them knowing about this?</i>

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:21.580
Reito-sama!

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.440
The train's almost here!

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:24.880
S-Sorry! I'm on my way!

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:30.050
<i>If I can use this to learn about
 the virus, I can make the cure!</i>

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:31.960
<b>Keimon City

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:33.020
Reito-sama! Hurry!

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:34.710
Sorry, I'm all set!

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.000
<i>I don't know who I can believe!</i>

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:49.460
No...

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.150
Stop it!

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:54.240
You're cute!

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.470
Knock it off!

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:57.980
Don't be such a prude.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.190
I know you're having fun 
with the other girls.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.420
No, stop!

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.550
Onee-sama!

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:13.750
Are you okay?

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.050
I'm fine.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:18.260
You haven't come to see me at all lately.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.310
I've been busy.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:22.430
Taking care of Mizuhara Reito, right?

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:29.530
Knowing you, I thought you'd 
moved on to some pretty UW girl.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.940
I didn't think a man would take you...

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.380
There's something I want you to do.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:35.360
Okay?

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:39.590
Anything for you, Onee-sama...

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:48.730
<i>I checked out the paper 
on making the MK Virus,</i>

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:53.090
<i>but some of the data was damaged and 
I couldn't recreate it immediately.</i>

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:56.960
<i>No, there's a limit to 
what I can do on my own.</i>

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.850
<i>I need other researchers helping me.</i>

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:01.370
Kuroda-san?

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:02.640
Wh-What?

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:06.400
Why is research on the 
MK Virus going so slowly?

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:10.740
There's barely any information on 
development of a vaccine or an antiviral.

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:13.900
I want to research it more, you know!

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:17.330
But they only let me research it a little.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:22.660
The technical director says we need to use 
our scientific resources on food production.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:26.510
And it's not that there's no 
research data on a vaccine.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:29.790
We're just not given access.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:36.190
And all the major researchers are 
at UW World Headquarters in America.

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:40.090
The people at the top of UW, 
the world's rulers,

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.880
are gathering virologists,

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:43.680
pharmacologists,

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:49.310
and high-end AI experts from all over
 the world to work on the research.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:55.950
I understand that with limited resources 
it makes more sense to centralize things,

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.700
but we have men who are up and moving now!

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.070
Japan needs more researchers, right?

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:04.950
Can't you bring back the 
Japanese researchers, at least?

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:08.060
I've asked my bosses a lot of times.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:10.130
Um, Mizuhara-sama...

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.280
You're...

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.040
I'm sorry to interrupt.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:15.710
There's something I wanted to ask you.

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:20.930
Hino-san wants Mahiru as a mating partner?!

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:23.310
Absolutely not!

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:28.400
I can't even imagine doing something 
naughty with a man I've never met!

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.480
She's still 16.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:31.810
I think it's too soon.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:35.230
Non-consensual mating is against the rules.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:38.080
Even if Number 1 wants it, it won't happen.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:40.420
I know that.

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:44.150
But I don't know if Hino-sama 
will give up so easily...

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:46.070
Go say no for me, Rei-nii!

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:47.260
What? Me?

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:48.710
I'd like you to, as well.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:54.290
If you tell him, Hino-sama 
will be more likely to agree.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:59.200
So I'm sorry...

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:00.550
Please!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.050
At least let me meet her!

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:04.590
If we meet, we might hit it off!

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.470
But she doesn't want to...

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.800
Please!

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:10.130
We can just have a drink and talk!

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:12.510
You've got lots of girls!

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:14.590
You don't need my little sister!

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:15.890
I fell in love at first sight!

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:16.940
Please!

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.670
Fine.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.160
I'll ask her.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.350
Hooray!

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:24.330
I'm glad you're such an 
understanding guy, Brother!

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.950
I'm not your brother!

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.650
But I can't promise, okay?

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.330
Fine!

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:33.500
Thank you, Brother! Thank you!

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:34.560
Quit it with the "Brother" stuff!

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:38.130
We're brothers forever now!

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:38.840
<i>This turned out weird...</i>

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:45.470
I see. So Mizuhara Mahiru 
refused to mate with Number 1.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.970
Yes. For now...

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:53.980
Hino-sama... Number 1... is not the type of 
guy to force himself on a girl, I believe.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.640
Understood. I'll leave that in your hands.

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:58.230
Next topic.

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:04.850
There was a small fight between a security 
patrol and the refugees in Area 15.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:06.120
Again?

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:07.490
There's been a lot of them, lately.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:13.110
It calmed down before it became a riot, 
but we need a large-scale solution, I think.

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:14.250
Yeah.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:18.640
More groups are starting to 
oppose UW in other countries.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:20.260
We need to do something.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.540
Maybe you're just too soft on them?

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:24.640
It's because there aren't enough rations.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:30.640
Why don't you stop doing weird research 
and make some high-nutrition GM foods?

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.510
What good comes from you fighting one another?

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.900
There's someone coming from HQ soon.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:38.180
I have a suggestion.

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:39.150
What?

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:41.900
Why not use Number 2?

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:46.690
If we have him distribute rations, 
it will calm the people down.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:48.530
Not a bad idea.

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:51.040
He's the most popular person in the world.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:52.990
I guess it's the only way.

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:55.420
Make sure security is tight.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:56.850
Of course.

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:08.680
Why don't you join us, Reito?

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.060
I'm sorry for this...

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:13.430
You're being watched.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:16.690
This is the only way we can talk to you.

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:21.690
Reito, you have some kind of information 
on the MK Virus, don't you?

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.950
You're looking into the virus 
outside the lab, too, aren't you?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:30.200
You should be more aware of how 
dangerous what you're doing is.

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:32.450
You could be killed.

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:36.330
Killed? By who?

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:39.210
I shouldn't need to tell you.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:43.870
For the past several years,

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:47.430
talented virologists have been 
vanishing, one after another.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:48.890
We don't know if they're alive or not.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.470
<i>Is that why Erisa...</i>

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.350
<i>This world is filled with lies.</i>

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:59.380
U-Um... Akane-san doesn't 
believe in the directors.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:02.380
I-I don't think it's true, but...

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:06.820
The leader of UW's Japan branch, 
the National Affairs Director, Kihara,

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:08.450
is my mother.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:13.870
Ryuuzouji is my father's name. 
He divorced my mom when I was little.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:15.560
I see.

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.520
I came to talk about rations distribution.

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:26.590
What are you doing?

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.160
Can't you tell?

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:31.470
We're seeing if Reito is healthy or not.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:34.280
I'd love to do some mating next.

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:38.100
S-Stop it! Don't pull that!

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.540
Maria, help!

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:45.070
Aww. You came and spoiled the fun.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:48.860
How stupid.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:54.700
Reito, you're going to visit 
the refugee areas, right?

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:55.670
Yes.

00:14:55.670 --> 00:15:01.290
They told me if I distributed the rations 
it would make people happy, so I agreed.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:02.660
Was that a mistake?

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:05.470
No. It's a good opportunity.

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:14.680
What do you want at this hour?

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:15.600
Mira...

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:19.340
You're so innocent. So beautiful.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:22.380
You know how I feel, don't you?

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:25.530
Ever since school, I've always loved you...

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:26.690
Stop it.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:29.590
I'm not your girlfriend.

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:38.000
I'll make you forget about that man soon.

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:50.260
Did you make sure that 
woman's not following you?

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:53.090
Rea-san's getting the rations ready.

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:56.150
It feels like a ghost could appear here.

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:57.350
It's fine.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:16:01.850
Making a hideout in the refugee 
area was a good idea, though.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:02.730
Right?

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:05.110
UW won't find us here.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:10.610
I can access external networks that 
are blocked off inside UW too, here.

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:15.070
You shouldn't trust the 
directors or Katagiri Rea.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:18.790
They're only interested in 
controlling this country.

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:25.660
Reito-sama! Look over here!

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.240
Reito-sama!

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:32.630
Hey, no pushing!

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.270
Stay in line!

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:35.640
No cutting!

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:37.880
He's so popular.

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:38.890
I don't like it.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:42.390
You mean UW? Or Mizuhara Reito?

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:43.580
Neither!

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:47.400
It's obvious they want to shut 
us up with food and a man.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:50.600
They're keeping all the food 
and the men to themselves!

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:52.280
Who do they think they are?

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.440
Hey, why don't we just leave town?

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:55.950
And go where?

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.030
I have a friend on the Sea of Japan side.

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:00.250
And she told me...

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:04.660
I can't believe I got to see you again!

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:07.540
I'm happy to hear that.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:08.790
Let's both do our best!

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:11.420
When will this end?

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:12.550
There's a lot more to go.

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:15.000
We'll be here all day!

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:45.960
I'm sorry, Onee-sama.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.750
I couldn't take her alive.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:49.600
Good work.

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:54.520
<i>I scanned their face, and there's 
nothing in the UW database.</i>

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:57.300
I'm pretty sure I know who it is.

00:17:57.580 --> 00:18:01.390
<i>I have some friends of 
mine watching the area,</i>

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:03.060
<i>and there don't seem to be any others.</i>

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:06.250
<i>Thanks. Keep an eye out.</i>

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:10.440
You seem quite concerned with Mizuhara Reito.

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.820
Did you fall in love?

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:15.360
I don't like him.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:19.560
But if he dies, it will make somebody sad.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:25.700
So nobody ends up coming to the concert,

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:28.760
and we start talking about 
breaking up the band.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:31.740
You're not interested at all, are you?

00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:32.730
Sorry.

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:36.740
Um... what kind of music 
do you like, Mahiru-chan?

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:38.440
I don't listen to music.

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:39.840
I see.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:40.840
Um...

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:42.360
I'll take your plates.

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:45.070
I'm not done...

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:50.480
How was Mizuhara Reito?

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.120
Just how he looks like on TV.

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:55.590
Maybe I'll switch from Kyouji-sama.

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:57.360
I'm not pregnant yet.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.280
Don't say that, even as a joke.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:04.380
Mizuhara Reito hasn't mated with anybody.

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:08.400
Does he not like girls?

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:10.580
Maybe he's into his sister?

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.890
Excuse me, can I order?

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:14.750
Coming.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:17.430
How much is she going to eat?

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:19.790
I'll be going.

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:21.410
I have something to do.

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:22.780
Hey, Mahiru!

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:25.300
Sorry about this.

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:26.980
Wait, Mahiru!

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.070
She rejected me!

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:36.530
I'm surprised you managed 
to find a computer this old.

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:40.150
We can only escape from UW's prying eyes

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.030
because we're using the 
old underground network.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.960
An underground network!

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:48.250
I didn't know you had hacking skills!

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:51.970
A-A friend from college was into this stuff.

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:54.170
She told me a lot.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:57.370
She's in America now, though.

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:01.310
Can we make contact with her 
and get their research data?

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.180
I think that would be difficult.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:07.680
UW's world HQ is even more 
locked down than Japan.

00:20:09.380 --> 00:20:11.690
That's Akane-san! I'll answer it!

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:12.940
Hey there—

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:17.940
Sorry, sorry!

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:20.570
I didn't think I'd scare you that much.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.940
Akane-san, what are you doing?

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:24.780
I need to disguise myself, you know!

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.550
You're standing out more!

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:36.210
Kyouji-sama, today was amazing...

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:52.730
You're really into the 
girl from yesterday, huh?

00:20:55.990 --> 00:20:57.730
That's not true.

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:07.630
Huh?

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:08.190
What's wrong?

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:09.490
L-Look at this!

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:13.990
<b>Kawakami Riona</b>

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:14.000
Kawakami Riona.
Keimon City Central Hospital #3.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:15.300
What's wrong with this?

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:18.000
M-My friend I just mentioned...

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:22.260
She was supposed to be in America, 
but it says she's hospitalized here.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:25.940
Yamagata Hatsumi.

00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:28.010
Keimon City Central Ward Hospital #3.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:31.140
Kimura Kana, Sakai Mayumi, Kurata Riyoko!

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:32.770
That's all of them!

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:35.520
All of them are researchers who 
are supposed to be in America!

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:39.770
And they've all gone missing 
in an abandoned hospital!

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:41.400
What's going on?

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:45.240
Girls with talents in pharmacology 
or medicine... So many...

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.830
They've all disappeared 
at the hospital where the

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:51.410
first MK Virus victim, 
Taniguchi-san's husband, was sent...

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:56.080
We may be getting a little 
too ahead of ourselves, but..

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:57.130
Say it.

00:21:56.640 --> 00:22:03.410
<b>Episode 6</b>

00:21:56.640 --> 00:22:03.410
<b>Intertwining Plots</b>

00:21:57.940 --> 00:22:04.910
<b>Keimon City Central Ward Hospital #3</b>

00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:03.730
This hospital may be where 
the MK Virus was first developed!

00:23:34.950 --> 01:00:00.000
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:23:34.950 --> 01:00:00.000
<b>Assigned to Me</b>
